WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.141 --> 00:00:02.645
(light upbeat music)

00:00:02.645 --> 00:00:03.800
- When I think about who I was as a person

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:07.040
before I came out, a lot
of it was me trying to be

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:09.280
this person that I knew that I wasn't.

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:10.480
- I think the most important word

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:13.380
that jumps out of me is closed off.

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:14.979
I think I was trying to hide so much.

00:00:14.979 --> 00:00:18.340
- I remember thinking
this was the worst thing

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:19.288
that could have happened to me

00:00:19.288 --> 00:00:21.411
and that God hated me,
or something like that.

00:00:21.411 --> 00:00:23.470
And I remember going to
church and being like;

00:00:23.470 --> 00:00:25.110
Oh my God, I don't know
what's wrong with me

00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:26.180
but I know I'm not normal.

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:27.380
Please help me out.

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:29.110
- I never really opened up to anyone.

00:00:29.110 --> 00:00:30.200
I had a really hard time.

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:32.132
Pretty much just kept a wall between me

00:00:32.132 --> 00:00:33.550
and even my closest friends.

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:36.714
If we ever were having a
conversation about being gay,

00:00:36.714 --> 00:00:40.700
I would always overreact and
be like; oh no, that's gross.

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:43.770
So people would absolutely
not think anything about me.

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:45.910
- In the job that I
had I worked in kind of

00:00:45.910 --> 00:00:48.370
a corporate world and I
didn't feel comfortable

00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:50.870
sharing my sexual identity with the people

00:00:50.870 --> 00:00:51.703
that I worked with.

00:00:51.703 --> 00:00:56.703
I would wear cute leather flats
and skirts and I hated it.

00:00:56.787 --> 00:01:00.130
It was what I thought I
need to do to survive.

00:01:00.130 --> 00:01:02.932
- I love things like
dance and figure skating.

00:01:02.932 --> 00:01:07.376
And I could speak the language
and I could play the game

00:01:07.376 --> 00:01:09.991
as far as how to present myself physically

00:01:09.991 --> 00:01:11.980
with clothes and makeup, and hair.

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:13.190
- Little things would trigger me back then

00:01:13.190 --> 00:01:15.670
to feel really uncomfortable
and really in my head.

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:17.880
For instance, I remember freshman year.

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:21.446
If I was sitting eating
lunch with a group of girls

00:01:21.446 --> 00:01:22.600
I would feel insecure

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:24.064
because I would feel like guys
were looking at me thinking;

00:01:24.064 --> 00:01:26.390
oh, look at that guy, he's fucking gay.

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:27.840
- I was very shy, I was very reserved.

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:29.770
I didn't like opening up to people.

00:01:29.770 --> 00:01:32.280
I always felt like I
couldn't be my true self.

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:34.320
I'd feel fine that I'm passing

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:36.410
and people aren't saying stuff about me.

00:01:36.410 --> 00:01:38.410
But on the inside, I would feel crushed.

00:01:39.510 --> 00:01:42.691
- A few years before I came
out I started dating a woman

00:01:42.691 --> 00:01:45.440
and in a very committed relationship

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:47.970
before anybody really knew.

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:49.534
Sometimes it felt like
we were playing pretend

00:01:49.534 --> 00:01:52.920
or that we couldn't hold hands
in public, or we couldn't

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:54.930
just be like; oh, let me tell
my friend about my girlfriend

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:56.340
'cause it's this really
cool and exciting thing

00:01:56.340 --> 00:01:57.600
that's happening in my life.

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:00.041
And not being able to do that for years

00:02:00.041 --> 00:02:02.040
just because I was afraid
of what was going to happen

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:04.780
was so hard.

00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:06.770
- It took a lot to convince myself

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:08.970
that I wasn't gonna to to hell.

00:02:08.970 --> 00:02:11.260
I had to do a lot of
work around those years

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:16.260
between 17 and 20, 21 to
really find out who I was

00:02:17.247 --> 00:02:20.393
on my own outside of all of those things.

00:02:20.393 --> 00:02:24.850
At a certain point I
couldn't keep lying anymore.

00:02:24.850 --> 00:02:27.145
I couldn't keep saying; no, that's not me.

00:02:27.145 --> 00:02:30.450
- I had a girlfriend
senior year of high school

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:32.100
that I very much liked.

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:33.270
For a long time I tried to hide it.

00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:35.299
I was like; well, if I can date a girl,

00:02:35.299 --> 00:02:38.530
I could just always ignore
the other side of me

00:02:38.530 --> 00:02:39.704
that's attracted to guys.

00:02:39.704 --> 00:02:40.960
Because I was still confused.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:43.710
I wasn't even sure what I
was or what I wanted to be.

00:02:43.710 --> 00:02:46.183
Me and her broke up and
I actually registered

00:02:46.183 --> 00:02:48.467
for a bunch of LGBT classes in college.

00:02:48.467 --> 00:02:52.069
Before I came out I wanted to
have resources and information

00:02:52.069 --> 00:02:54.680
so that people couldn't tear me down.

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:56.570
Once I understood that I wasn't wrong,

00:02:56.570 --> 00:02:58.040
then I was like; okay,
I'm ready to come out

00:02:58.040 --> 00:03:00.070
and if somebody wants to
challenge me, I'm gonna be like;

00:03:00.070 --> 00:03:01.790
no, here is why.

00:03:01.790 --> 00:03:03.540
I know what the fuck
is going on in my head.

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:05.625
- My mom was the biggest
person I knew I needed to tell

00:03:05.625 --> 00:03:08.230
before I could feel like
I officially came out.

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:09.860
And it could go one of two ways.

00:03:09.860 --> 00:03:12.020
Either she would see me as her daughter

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:14.189
and she would love me
and it would be okay.

00:03:14.189 --> 00:03:16.164
Or the horror stories that you hear.

00:03:16.164 --> 00:03:19.517
I was bouncing back and forth
between those two thoughts

00:03:19.517 --> 00:03:22.350
of I hope she still loves me.

00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:25.270
- Before coming out to my
family and the world at large

00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:29.480
was slowly coming out and
finding other adults in the world

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:31.327
that I could talk to
who were very accepting.

00:03:31.327 --> 00:03:34.830
Other out queer people, adults,

00:03:34.830 --> 00:03:39.830
and finding a reference point
so I knew that no matter what

00:03:40.090 --> 00:03:41.930
I had a future, that I was gonna be okay.

00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:44.240
That even in my community,
even if I didn't see

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:46.710
those role models, those people
thriving, I knew that they

00:03:46.710 --> 00:03:47.650
were out there somewhere.

00:03:47.650 --> 00:03:48.840
I just had to get out there.

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:50.190
- I finally got to a
point in my relationship

00:03:50.190 --> 00:03:53.358
where I knew we weren't gonna
get anywhere until I came out,

00:03:53.358 --> 00:03:55.170
until we both came out.

00:03:55.170 --> 00:03:57.690
And it's gonna suck, and it might hurt,

00:03:57.690 --> 00:03:59.850
and it might be really
detrimental to some relationships

00:03:59.850 --> 00:04:02.800
in our lives, but it's gonna
be better in the long run.

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:04.640
I was in a safe space, I
was in a safe environment

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:06.040
where I was able to come out.

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:09.897
And I was fortunate enough
to have a mom who listened.

00:04:09.897 --> 00:04:11.069
- The way I came out to my mom,

00:04:11.069 --> 00:04:12.807
she took it the hardest out of everyone.

00:04:12.807 --> 00:04:17.370
But I felt like I had the
resources to help her understand

00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:18.728
what it was and what it meant.

00:04:18.728 --> 00:04:21.630
And help her through this
process because I understand

00:04:21.630 --> 00:04:22.980
that for her it's probably really hard.

00:04:22.980 --> 00:04:25.977
- So we were actually on a
long two hourish car ride home.

00:04:25.977 --> 00:04:27.730
I really need to get this off my chest.

00:04:27.730 --> 00:04:28.960
Everything I pretty much thought

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:31.028
she would think and say, she did.

00:04:31.028 --> 00:04:33.970
At points it got even worse

00:04:33.970 --> 00:04:35.686
that what I thought it would get.

00:04:35.686 --> 00:04:37.064
It was pretty devastating.

00:04:37.064 --> 00:04:39.900
It's the kind of stuff that
you hear in media all the time

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:44.000
and in TV of these extreme
stories about families

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:45.320
kicking their kids out for being gay.

00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:47.031
Or just saying these really awful things.

00:04:47.031 --> 00:04:50.340
To hear that coming out
of your own mom's mouth

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:51.800
is almost a surreal experience.

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:53.260
Even though it didn't
go the way I was hoping,

00:04:53.260 --> 00:04:54.462
it still helped me grow as a person

00:04:54.462 --> 00:04:56.140
and I wouldn't trade it for the world.

00:04:56.140 --> 00:04:59.920
- I can't imagine my adult
life without coming out.

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:03.723
I can't imagine if I was still that person

00:05:03.723 --> 00:05:06.136
that I was trying to pretend to be.

00:05:06.136 --> 00:05:10.112
And I think the difference
between then verses now

00:05:10.112 --> 00:05:12.450
is that I'm my full self.

00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:14.980
- Now I finally get to really figure out

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:16.908
who I am as a person.

00:05:16.908 --> 00:05:19.583
And who I'm gonna be as a
person for the rest of my life.

00:05:19.583 --> 00:05:23.360
Being gay isn't just about who you like

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:24.510
and who you're attracted to.

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:27.700
And when you feel
comfortable in your clothes

00:05:27.700 --> 00:05:29.840
and in your skin, people can tell.

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:31.680
And I think you look
through life differently

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:33.506
and you walk through
life more confidently.

00:05:33.506 --> 00:05:36.690
And for me it's really changed who I am.

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:39.430
- People would be drawn to
me more because those walls

00:05:39.430 --> 00:05:41.730
that I had built and kept up for so long

00:05:41.730 --> 00:05:44.470
for people to not know anything about me

00:05:44.470 --> 00:05:47.280
was starting to fade and
people could see the real me

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:48.630
and they gravitated toward that.

00:05:48.630 --> 00:05:49.600
And it made me feel good

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:52.390
that people can genuinely like me for me.

00:05:52.390 --> 00:05:55.054
- The biggest thing for me
has been the acceptance that

00:05:55.054 --> 00:05:56.621
people have for you.

00:05:56.621 --> 00:05:58.170
Now I'm just myself.

00:05:58.170 --> 00:05:59.340
I think I'm just more relaxed.

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:01.850
It really, really is a
weight off your shoulders.

00:06:01.850 --> 00:06:03.135
- We all think we have crazy dreams.

00:06:03.135 --> 00:06:05.910
But if you really believe
that this is something

00:06:05.910 --> 00:06:07.510
that's genuine for you and true for you,

00:06:07.510 --> 00:06:08.782
and something that you really want,

00:06:08.782 --> 00:06:10.269
you should never stop yourself.

00:06:10.269 --> 00:06:12.730
Just know that there's other
people like you out there.

00:06:12.730 --> 00:06:16.170
Please find other people that
can be your support system.

00:06:16.170 --> 00:06:18.320
- Coming out means that you're ready

00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:20.230
to just tell the world what you are.

00:06:20.230 --> 00:06:22.220
And sometimes you're not,
sometimes you don't even know

00:06:22.220 --> 00:06:23.053
what you are.

00:06:23.053 --> 00:06:24.380
It takes years to find out what you are.

00:06:24.380 --> 00:06:25.580
And it's okay for you to say;

00:06:25.580 --> 00:06:27.080
I'm figuring it out and we'll see.

00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:27.913
And if you don't feel

00:06:27.913 --> 00:06:29.660
like it's safe for you to come out, don't.

00:06:29.660 --> 00:06:31.420
But do work with yourself.

00:06:31.420 --> 00:06:33.410
If you're struggling with
coming out, there's no rush.

00:06:33.410 --> 00:06:34.280
Time your time.

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:35.781
- There's no one right way to do it.

00:06:35.781 --> 00:06:38.890
It might go really well, it
might not go really well.

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:41.577
It is a moment that you
deserve to choose for yourself.

00:06:41.577 --> 00:06:44.650
Never let anyone make you
feel like you have to come out

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:45.642
when you're not ready to.

00:06:45.642 --> 00:06:48.020
I hope it's something that
everyone gets to experience.

00:06:48.020 --> 00:06:49.720
And if you don't get to experience that

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:52.833
because you're not in a
place or a position to do so,

00:06:52.833 --> 00:06:55.420
then that's okay, we still love you.

00:06:55.420 --> 00:06:57.570
You are still part of this community.

00:06:57.570 --> 00:06:59.880
And you are no less recognized for it.

00:06:59.880 --> 00:07:02.117
You are no less of a queer person for it.

00:07:02.117 --> 00:07:06.392
And we're here to celebrate
who you are as a person

00:07:06.392 --> 00:07:09.440
regardless of whether
you can come out or not.

00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:11.150
- There's a mountain of obstacles.

00:07:11.150 --> 00:07:14.845
But if you keep trying and
you keep talking to people,

00:07:14.845 --> 00:07:17.940
and you keep reaching out,
and you keep working as hard

00:07:17.940 --> 00:07:20.623
as you possibly can,
you will find your spot.

00:07:20.623 --> 00:07:23.270
And you will find your safe space.

00:07:23.270 --> 00:07:24.762
It is out there.

00:07:24.762 --> 00:07:26.810
Do not give up.

